{"status":"answered","explanation":"The evidence indicates Pliny requested an architect or someone skilled in waterworks construction because the existing aqueduct projects had failed, and he suggested that sending such a person would be necessary for the new design. Trajan required Pliny to examine the misconduct regarding the large sums spent on the aqueduct and to ensure the city of Nicomedia was supplied with water.","claims":[{"text":"Pliny requested an architect or someone skilled in waterworks construction because the previous aqueduct attempts had failed and he believed it would be necessary for the new design to succeed.", "citations":[{"id":"pliny:XLVI:1","path":"vault/raw/pliny.html#link2H_4_0157","quote":"But that this work may not meet with the same ill-success as the former, it will be necessary to send here an architect, or some one skilled in the construction of this kind of waterworks."}
]},{"text":"Trajan required Pliny to examine the misconduct concerning the large sums spent on the aqueduct to ensure the money was not applied to private purposes.", "citations":[{"id":"pliny:XLVII:1","path":"vault/raw/pliny.html#link2H_4_0158","quote":"But really it is no less incumbent upon you to examine by whose misconduct it has happened that such large sums have been thrown away upon this, lest they apply the money to private purposes, and the aqueduct in question, like the preceding, should be begun, and afterwards left unfinished."}
]}]}

